  "The common feature of cultural exchanges with China and the region is the parallel existence of two opposing trends. They are:\nA. On the one hand is the tendency to be influenced by Han culture and on the other side is the tendency to anti-Han and Vietnamize Chinese influences.\nB. On the one hand is the tendency to be influenced by Han culture and on the other side is the tendency to anti-Han.\nC. On the one hand is the tendency to be influenced by Han culture and the other side is Vietnamize Chinese influences.\nD. All are incorrect\nA",
  "The cultural period of the anti-Northern colonial period started in BC and lasted until Ngo Quyen regained the country. The main features of this cultural period are:\nA. Consciousness of indomitable and permanent resistance to the threat of invasion from Northern feudalism, the decline of Van Lang - Au Lac civilization and the opening the process of exchange and reception of Chinese and regional cultures\nB. Consciousness of indomitable and permanent resistance to the threat of invasion from Northern feudalism and the flourishing of Van Lang - Au Lac civilization\nC. The deliberate destruction of the northern invaders with a malicious assimilation scheme and the regular natural degradation of a culture after reaching its peak\nD. All are correct\nA",
  "What are the characteristics of Dai Nam culture?\nA. For the first time, our country achieved unification in terms of territory and administrative organization from Dong Van to Ca Mau.\nB. After the chaotic period Le-Mac, Trinh-Nguyen, came to the Nguyen Dynasty. Confucianism was restored as the state religion, but it gradually declined.\nC. The beginning of the process of penetration of Western culture, is also the beginning of the period when Vietnamese culture integrates into human culture.\nD. All are correct\nD",
  "What are the characteristics of Dong Son culture?\nA. Traveling by water transport\nB. The beliefs of fertility, worship of nature, worship of ancestors and heroes.\nC. Cultural exchange between tribes.\nD. All are correct\nD",
  "Dai Viet period became the second highest peak in Vietnamese cultural history with two milestones:\nA. Ly- Tran Dynasty and Hau Le Dynasty\nB. Ly Dynasty and Tran Dynasty\nC. Le Dynasty and Nguyen Dynasty\nD. All are incorrect\nA",
  "Which of the following is of international significance?\nA. Van hoa\nB. Van minh\nC. Van hien\nD. Van vat\nB",
  "What race of people were the inhabitants of ancient Southeast Asia?\nA. Indonésien\nB. Austroasiatic\nC. Austronésien\nD. Australoid\nA",
  "Specific product of Dong Nai culture is:\nA. Beast head earrings (khuyen tai dau thu)\nB. Terracotta Jar coffin (mo chum gom)\nC. Gold jewelry\nD. Stone musical instrument\nD",
  "In what period was Confucianism brought up as the state religion in Vietnam?\nA. Dinh - Le Dynasty\nB. Ly - Tran Dynasty\nC. Hau Le Dynasty\nD. Nguyen Dynasty\nC",
  "Dai Viet was named by the king of which dynasty?\nA. Ly Dynasty\nB. Tran Dynasty\nC. Le Dynasty\nD. Dinh Dynasty\nA",
  "Regarding the characteristics of traditional Vietnamese urban organizations, which of the following statements is not true?\nA. Cities are created by the state, mainly performing administrative functions.\nB. The city is influenced by the countryside and has a strong rural character.\nC. Cities formed spontaneously.\nD. Cities are always at risk of being rural.\nC",
  "The basic principles that assemble human beings into society, making them social creatures are:\nA. Same location\nB. Same origin\nC. Same benefits.\nD. All are correct\nD",
  "Which culture plays a decisive role in establishing Vietnamese cultural identity?\nA. Son Vi culture\nB. Hoa Binh culture\nC. Dong Son culture\nD. Sa Huynh culture\nC",
  "In what period was the Thang Long citadel divided into 36 wards?\nA. Ly- Tran Dynasty\nB. Hau Le Dynasty\nC. Nguyen Dynasty\nD. Tien Le Dynasty\nB",
  "Which of the following statements is correct?\nA. The process of formation and development of Dong Son culture in the North is the process of forming the core of the ancient Viet people and the first state of the ancient Viet people.\nB. The process of formation and development of Dong Son culture in the South is the process of forming the core of the ancient Viet people and the first state of the ancient Viet people.\nC. The process of formation and development of Hoa Binh culture in the North is the process of forming the core of the ancient Viet people and the first state of the ancient Viet people.\nD. The process of formation and development of Nui Do culture in the North is the process of forming the core of the ancient Viet people and the first state of the ancient Viet people.\nA",
  "During the Le Dynasty, Thang Long citadel was divided into how many wards?\nA. 61\nB. 36\nC. 31\nD. 63\nB",
  "Confucianism is:\nA. An economic theory\nB. A moral political doctrine\nC. An ideology only for the unorthodox feudal state.\nD. A philosophical doctrine\nB",
  "In which year did the exam system in Chinese characters end in Tonkin?\nA. 1918\nB. 1917\nC. 1916\nD. 1915\nD",
  "Which century marked the end of Confucianism?\nA. XVI\nB. XVII\nC. XVIII\nD. XIX\nD",
  "Which of the following religions arose from the South?\nA. Cao Dai, Taoism, Buddhism\nB. Protestantism, Hoa Hao\nC. Cao Dai, Hoa Hao\nD. All are incorrect\nC",
  "The meaning of fertility beliefs is:\nA. Wishing all good luck and abundance throughout the year.\nB. Doing magic for a bountiful harvest.\nC. Wishing to have many children.\nD. Wishing a bountiful harvest and having many children.\nD",
  "During which cultural period were the currents of bourgeois democracy and Marxist-Leninist ideology transmitted to Vietnam?\nA. Culture of the Northern feudal period\nB. Culture of Dai Viet period\nC. Culture of Dai Nam period\nD. Culture of Modern period\nC",
  "The owners of the Oc Eo culture are:\nA. Residents speak Tay- Thai language\nB. Residents speak Mon- Khome language\nC. Residents speak Han- Tang language\nD. Residents speak Nam Dao language\nD",
  "The characteristics of Dong Nai culture are:\nA. Farming and crafts.\nB. Typical cultural achievements: Rock musical instruments (Dan da)\nC. Popular occupations: growing rice on land, farming, hunting\nD. All are correct\nD",
  "The Hong Duc law marks an important development in the history of the rule of law in Vietnam. When was this law enacted?\nA. Ly Dynasty\nB. Tran Dynasty\nC. Hau Le Dynasty\nD. Nguyen Dynasty\nC",
  "The main production field of Viet Co people is:\nA. Agriculture- Planting crops\nB. Traditional crafts: bronze casting, pottery, stone carving, wood carving, knitting...\nC. Growing rice agriculture.\nD. Raising livestock and poultry\nC",
  "What was the main purpose of the French to maintain the organization of villages and communes (the basic social structure) when they invaded our country?\nA. As a place to teach Vietnamese to the French.\nB. Easy to control residents.\nC. Local agricultural development.\nD. Using the feudal apparatus to do jobs for the colonial government.\nD",
  "Champa culture belongs to which cultural region?\nA. Bac Bo- The North\nB. Trung Bo- The Central\nC. Viet Bac\nD. Tay Bac- The Northwest\nB",
  "Which culture plays the role of the original culture of the Southern region?\nA. Champa\nB. Oc Eo\nC. Sa Huynh\nD. Dong Son\nB",
  "Confucianism was formed in which country?\nA. Thailand\nB. India\nC. China\nD. Vietnam\nC",
  "The main feature in the life of Champa kings is:\nA. Vishnu religion\nB. Shiva religion\nC. Brahma religion\nD. Buddhism\nB",
  "Which king of the Nguyen Dynasty chose Hue as the capital instead of Thang Long?\nA. Gia Long\nB. Minh Mang\nC. Thieu Tri\nD. Tu Duc\nA",
  "In which year was Thang Long Imperial Citadel built?\nA. 1010\nB. 1070\nC. 1011\nD. 1007\nA",
  "Dong Son bronze drum is the achievement of which cultural period?\nA. Prehistoric\nB. Van Lang- Au Lac\nC. The Northern feudal\nD. Dai Viet\nB",
