  "In 1075, the court of King Ly Nhan Tong organized the first exam to select talented people to be mandarins. The first place winner in that exam is:\nA. Le Van Huu\nB. Chu Van An\nC. Le Van Thinh\nD. Nguyen Hien\nC",
  "Which cultural feature does not belong to the period from 1858 to 1945?\nA. Forced contact and cultural interference between Vietnam and France.\nB. The development to the pinnacle of Chinese literature.\nC. Natural cultural exchange between Vietnam and the East-West world.\nD. Journalism was born and developed.\nB",
  "The Nguyen Dynasty located the capital in:\nA. Hue\nB. Nghe An\nC. Ha Noi\nD. Quang Nam\nA",
  "What image is the traditional symbol of autonomy in Vietnamese villages?\nA. Bamboo\nB. Village communal courtyard\nC. Banyan Tree\nD. Rive\nA",
  "\"The Northern feudal period\" is named for which period by historians?\nA. 1407- 1427\nB. XV- XIX\nC. I- X\nD. 500 years BC\nC",
  "What occupations were Thuy Chuong and Nghi Tam wards famous for in the Le dynasty?\nA. Paper making\nB. Pottery making\nC. Bronze casting\nD. Fabric and silk weaving\nD",
  "Popular housing type of residents of Dong Son culture is:\nA. House on a boat\nB. House on land\nC. House on raft\nD. Stilt house\nD",
  "Which is INCORRECT about Animism under pre-colonial times?\nA. Based on the merits, the court ordained the gods of the Citadel according to levels.\nB. The imperial states regulated Animistic practices to legitimize imperial rule and prevent 'ta giao' (\"heterodox teaching\") from corrupting morals and promoting rebellion.\nC. Each village has had a 'dinh', or communal house, used for council meetings and rituals honoring the 'than hoang', the village's patron deity.\nD. None of the above\nD",
  "Which one of the following statements about the Yin Yang Symbol in Taoism is INCORRECT?\nA. The dots in the Yin Yang symbol indicate that there is no absolute yin or yang, each contains the germ of the other.\nB. The outer circle indicates that all things are made up of yin and yang.\nC. The duality of yin and yang is an indivisible whole.\nD. Yang refers to negative/passive/female principles in nature.\nD",
  "Who founded Buddhism?\nA. Siddhartha Gautama\nB. Shakyamuni\nC. The \"Buddha\"\nD. All are correct\nD",
  "The Basic Teachings of Buddha which are core to Buddhism are\nA. The Three Universal Truths\nB. The Four Noble Truths\nC. The Noble Eightfold Path\nD. All are correct\nD",
  "Which of the following are beliefs of Buddhism?\nB. (1) and (2)\nC. (2) and (3)\nD. (1), (2), (3), and (4)\nD",
  "When was Buddhism first introduced to Vietnam (came from China)?\nA. In the 1st century C.E\nB. In the Ly dynasty (11 century)\nC. In about 500 B.C.E\nD. In the 7th century\nA",
