  "Three Virtues every Vietnamese Buddhist Youth Association member and leader are advised to follow:\nA. Compassion\nB. Wisdom\nC. Bravery\nD. All are correct\nD",
  "Which of the following statements is not true about Confucianism?\nA. Be a system of thought and behavior originating in ancient China.\nB. Confucianism is not a religion that is based upon the belief in a personalized God.\nC. Confucianism concerns the issues of gods, spirits, and death.\nD. Confucianism emphasizes the feeling of piety.\nC",
  "Which belong to the Five Relationships of Confucianism?\nA. (1), (2), (3), and (4)\nB. (1), (2), and (4)\nC. (2), (3), (4), and (5)\nD. (1), (3), (4), and (5)\nA",
  "Which of the following statements about Confucianism in Vietnam is CORRECT?\nA. Confucianism was introduced into Vietnam early during Chinese rule and has maintained its influence since that time.\nB. In 1075, the first Confucian exam was opened with the names \"Confucian Studies\" and \"Three Schools of Confucianism\", officially giving birth to the long history of Confucian examinations in Vietnam.\nC. The idea of territorial sovereignty identified in Ly Thuong Kiet's Nam Quoc Son Ha is considered to be influenced by Confucian thought.\nD. All are correct\nD",
  "Which is NOT included in The Seven Sacraments?\nA. Baptism\nB. Eucharist\nC. Reconciliation\nD. Recognition\nD",
  "Which of the following statements about Catholicism in Vietnam is INCORRECT?\nA. The Catholic Church flourished under the colonialists' patronage, opening missions, schools, and hospitals all over the country, and becoming Vietnam's largest landowner.\nB. Vietnamese Catholics were favored above their compatriots and became an educated elite under French Domination.\nC. Under King Minh Mang, Catholicism flourished.\nD. After reunification, the communists placed restrictions on the Catholic Church and imprisoned several of its leaders who had actively opposed the new government.\nC",
  "Who created Cao Dai?\nA. Ngo Van Chieu\nB. Vietnamese Catholics were favored above their compatriots and became an educated elite under French Domination.\nC. Ngo Dinh Nhu\nD. Ngo Van Vo\nA",
  "Who does Caodaism worship?\nA. God the Father\nB. Holy Mother\nC. The Divine Beings\nD. All are correct\nD",
  "When was Caodaism officially established?\nA. In 1919\nB. In 1926\nC. In 1924\nD. In 1950\nB",
  "Which of the following statement about Hoa Hao Buddhism is INCORRECT?\nA. It was founded in 1939\nB. A Hoa Hao Buddhist practicing Buddhism for self-improvement must, first of all, do his best to comply with the Four Great Debts Of Gratitude.\nC. Hoa Hao was a powerful independent force in South Vietnamese politics until the final victory of the communists in 1975.\nD. Hoa Hao followers are required to shave their heads and take refuge in pagodas.\nD",
  "There are 4 holy animals known as Vietnamese cultural symbols. They are:\nA. Dragons, Turtles, Phoenix, Unicorn\nB. Dragons, Tigers, Phoenix, Unicorn\nC. Dragons, Turtles, Phoenix, Lions\nD. All are correct\nA",
