  "In which country did Taoism originate?\nA. Thailand\nB. India\nC. Vietnam\nD. China\nD",
  "Similarities between religion and belief are:\nA. Massive ideology\nB. Belief in things that are invisible and have the function of regulating society.\nC. Well- organized and taught by education.\nD. There are heads, believers, praying at the synagogue.\nB",
  "How many categories may Vietnamese Literature be separated into?\nA. 2\nB. 3\nC. 4\nD. 5\nB",
  "Which does not belong to Vietnamese Literature Categories?\nA. Written in Chinese characters\nB. Written in Vernacular characters\nC. Written in Egyptian hieroglyphs\nD. Written in Romanized Script\nC",
  "Choose the NOT TRUE statement The Folk Tradition\nA. The main purpose of folklore is to convey a moral lesson and present useful information and daily life lessons in an easy way for the common people to understand.\nB. The origins of the folk tradition cannot be precisely dated.\nC. The folk literature is always recorded in writing and passed from one generation to the next.\nD. The Intelligent buffalo' is an example of Folktale.\nC",
  "Choose the CORRECT statement\nA. 'Collected Poems in the National Language' was written in Vernacular characters.\nB. The Vernacular characters were developed based on Latin characters.\nC. 'Nom' prevented authors from producing works that drew upon the popular traditions.\nD. None of the above\nA",
  "Which was the work not written in Vernacular characters?\nA. \"Compilation of Bach Van's Poems\" by Nguyen Binh Khiem\nB. \"Lament of a Warrior's Wife\" by Dang Tran Con\nC. \"Lament of a Royal Concubine\" by Nguyen Gia Thieu\nD. \"Doctor Pig\" and \"Doctor Quynh\" by Ho Xuan Huong\nB",
  "When was the golden age for 'chu Nom'?\nA. 18th century\nB. 16th century\nC. 15th century\nD. 19th century\nA",
