  "In 1961, during an excavation, archaeologists discovered wooden artifacts coated with lacquer and animal skins, providing evidence of the existence of lacquer techniques in the northern Red River Delta region since when?\nA. 4th century BC\nB. 5th century BC\nC. 6th century BC\nD. 7th century BC\nA",
