  "How did the specialization of labor among villages in the Red River Delta contribute to the production process of handicrafts?\nA. It slowed down the production process due to the need for transportation between villages.\nB. It allowed each village to master a specific step, creating an efficient artisanal chain of production.\nC. It limited the creativity of artisans as they were confined to only one aspect of production.\nD. It caused economic instability as villages became dependent on one another for survival.\nB",
  "Choose the CORRECT words to fill in the bank: The Temple of Literature (Van Mieu) was dedicated to..., and its grounds served as a royal college.\nA. Buddhism\nB. Taoism\nC. Confucius\nD. None of these answers\nC",
