  "At Tet (Lunar New Year), in the past, the elders often wished each other: \"At the beginning of the year, have a .... ; at the end of the year, have a ...\"\nA. Son Daughter\nB. Daughter-Son\nC. Granddaughter - Grandson\nD. Grandson-Granddaughter\nA",
  "What do Vietnamese people like to do while eating to make the meal enjoyable?\nA. Eat very fast\nB. Don't eat too fast, don't eat too slow\nC. Place chopsticks on bowl while eating\nD. Dig chopsticks into food to choose delicious pieces\nE. Talk loudly while eating and make phone calls\nB",
