  "According to the cultural researcher Huu Ngoc's account in the book Wandering through Vietnamese Culture (World Publishing House, 2017), In Hanoi during the French colonial period, what items did many well-off middle-class families often display on their tea cabinets?\nA. The Three Deities of Happiness, Prosperity, and Longevity\nB. Set of horizontal lacquered board and parallel scrolls\nC. Carved wooden furniture set\nD. Set of \"Four Noble Plants\" paintings\nA",
