  "What is the primary difference between \"Nhac Tai tu\" in southern Vietnam and Ca Hue in central Vietnam?\nA. \"Nhạc Tai tu\" evolved into a more amateur, intimate form of music played by aficionados, while Ca Hue is more formal and courtly.\nB. \"Nhạc Tai tu\" is more instrumental and formal than Ca Hue.\nC. \"Nhạc Tai tu\" is performed only by professional musicians, while Ca Hue is a more folk tradition.\nD. \"Nhạc Tai tu\" focuses more on vocal performance than instrumental music.\nA",
